+// An unpackaged launch declares no application identifier, so Windows groups its taskbar
+// button — and the shortcut "Pin to taskbar" writes — under electron.exe: the entry reads
+// "Electron" and the pin relaunches a bare Electron window. A stable AppUserModelID here,
+// matching the shortcut, gives the running window and that shortcut one taskbar identity.
+// The packaged build keeps the identifier electron-builder derives from its own appId.
+if (process.platform === 'win32' && !app.isPackaged) app.setAppUserModelId('com.deepseek.harness.dev')
